---
import ContentGrid from "../structure/ContentGrid.astro";
import ContentSection from "../structure/ContentSection.astro";
---

<ContentSection id="library" title="Seattle reference library" headingLevel="h2">
<p>
      Keeping old equipment working takes more than spare parts. We rely on
      diagrams, manuals, and the knowledge people wrote down while these
      systems were in service. Our cataloged reference library focuses on
      Seattle, the Pacific Northwest, and the machines we maintain.
    </p>

    <ContentGrid columns={2}>
      <r-cell>
        <ContentSection id="using-the-library" title="Using the library" headingLevel="h3">
          <p>
            We try to make our printed telecommunications history and technical
            documentation available to researchers and the wider telephone
            collector community. Digitization of technical material is
            available on request. Tell us what you're looking for at
            <a href="mailto:library@connections.museum">library@connections.museum</a>.
          </p>
        </ContentSection>
      </r-cell>
      <r-cell>
        <ContentSection id="contributing-material" title="Contributing material" headingLevel="h3">
          <p>
            Have documents about Pacific Northwest telephone history or the
            panel switch, especially anything marked “Full Mechanical”? Please
            email <a href="mailto:library@connections.museum">library@connections.museum</a>
            with a description before sending them. We don't yet have a
            dedicated archival environment in Seattle, so knowing what you
            have helps us find the right way to care for it.
          </p>
        </ContentSection>
      </r-cell>
    </ContentGrid>
</ContentSection>
